      "heading": "Course Fees and the 10 Percent Test",
      "content": {
        "kind": "items",
        "items": [
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "A career objective for a business development or business management resume should say in two or three lines which role you want, what you can already do and what kind of result you aim for, and it works only when the rest of the resume carries evidence for each claim."
          },
          {
            "heading": "",
            "text": "Never claim a skill, target or result you cannot explain in an interview."
          }
        ]
      },
